# Baron Helmut Zemo (3/3 for {B}{B}{B}): "Boast - Exile any number of black cards from your graveyard with fifteen or more black mana
# symbols among their mana costs: Copy those exiled cards. You may cast up to three of the copies without paying their mana
# costs." Two Entombs, cast on turn 1, put Doomsday Excruciator ({B}x6) and Pox Plague ({B}x5) into Bot1's graveyard; Zemo comes
# down on turn 3. On turn 5 the third Entomb takes a Swamp (no colour, no symbols) and Zemo's connive discards Griselbrand (4), so
# the graveyard holds three Entombs (a black symbol each), the Excruciator, Pox Plague, Griselbrand and the Swamp. Zemo cannot
# boast until it attacks. The cards chosen must be black and have fifteen or more symbols between them: the Excruciator, Pox Plague
# and the three Entombs (6 + 5 + 3 = 14) are refused, so is the Swamp with fifteen, and the Excruciator, Pox Plague and
# Griselbrand (exactly 15) are exiled. Of the three copies, Bot1 casts the Griselbrand one - it becomes a token - and stops; the
# other two copies cease to exist and the cards stay in exile.

